        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the pot by holding BOTH the best 5-card poker hand AND the highest spade among all players at showdown.',
          gameplay: 'Seven card stud deal: two cards face down, four face up, one face down. Five betting rounds, one after each round of face-up cards and one after the final card. At showdown, to win the pot a player must have both the best five-card poker hand and the highest spade among all players; the highest spade may be any of the seven cards, not necessarily face down. If the best hand and the highest spade are held by different players, or if no one has a spade, no one wins and the pot carries over to the next deal. Only players who were in the showdown participate in the carryover deal.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must hold BOTH best hand AND highest spade to win.',
            'If conditions are split between players, pot carries over.',
            'Carried-over pot grows across multiple deals â€” can become enormous.',
            'Only showdown participants play the next deal when pot carries over.',
            'Highest spade uses ANY of the 7 cards, not just hole cards.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Value spades highly. A hand with the Ace of Spades in the hole is extremely powerful â€” it guarantees the highest-spade requirement. Focus on building the best hand while holding strong spades.',
          intermediate: "Track spades on the board: if the Aâ™  is visible in someone's up-cards, they have a huge advantage. If most high spades are mucked or visible, estimate which spades remain in play. With no spades in your hand, you literally cannot win â€” fold unless you can improve.",
          advanced: "The carryover mechanic changes strategy dramatically when the pot is large. Players with high spades in the hole should play aggressively to build a monster pot they can scoop. Monitor opponents' visible spades to assess whether the pot will likely carry over or be claimed.",
          tips: [
            'Aâ™  in the hole is nearly unbeatable for the spade requirement â€” play aggressively.',
            'With no spades in hand by 5th street, folding is usually correct.',
            'Multiple carryovers create massive pots â€” the game becomes very high-stakes quickly.',
            "Track all visible spades carefully to estimate your spade's ranking.",
          ],
